  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Original flattened near-tetrapod fish fossil with preserved digit-bearing fin anatomy, MHNM06-2067-informed study. A volumetric low-poly fossil relief with genuine discrete fin elements, not a photograph/painted plane and not a free-standing living animal. [\"Original fossil is compressed; low-poly relief height and soft connecting silhouette are representational.\", \"Fig3e attempts restoration of compressed element shapes; prefer Fig3d actual CT configuration rather than silently claiming restored bones are exact.\", \"Fine scale/ray counts simplified; no scientific claim of pixel-accurate CT segmentation.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"fossil_total_length_m\": 1.57, \"status\": \"Published specimen total length, Nature2020 abstract. Fig1a scale1m; fin Figs2–3 scales5cm.\", \"estimated_body_width_m\": 0.25, \"slab_length_m\": 1.67, \"slab_width_m\": 0.42, \"relief_height_m\": 0.025, \"uncertainty\": \"Slab geometry and relief depth are artist-controlled support dimensions, not measured original slab thickness. Preserve body/fin scale relationship.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Original flattened near-tetrapod fish fossil with preserved digit-bearing fin anatomy, MHNM06-2067-informed study. A volumetric low-poly fossil relief with genuine discrete fin elements, not a photograph/painted plane and not a free-standing living animal. [\"Original fossil is compressed; low-poly relief height and soft connecting silhouette are representational.\", \"Fig3e attempts restoration of compressed element shapes; prefer Fig3d actual CT configuration rather than silently claiming restored bones are exact.\", \"Fine scale/ray counts simplified; no scientific claim of pixel-accurate CT segmentation.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"fossil_total_length_m\": 1.57, \"status\": \"Published specimen total length, Nature2020 abstract. Fig1a scale1m; fin Figs2–3 scales5cm.\", \"estimated_body_width_m\": 0.25, \"slab_length_m\": 1.67, \"slab_width_m\": 0.42, \"relief_height_m\": 0.025, \"uncertainty\": \"Slab geometry and relief depth are artist-controlled support dimensions, not measured original slab thickness. Preserve body/fin scale relationship.\"}"
  },
